    <!-- TAB 2: ABSTRACT REVIEW -->
    <section id="section-abstracts" class="hidden space-y-6">
      <!-- How many abstracts have their full author list, with a filter for
           the rest. renderAbstractsAuthorsSummary(). -->
      <div id="abstracts-authors-summary" class="hidden flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2 rounded-xl border border-gold-300 bg-gold-50 px-4 py-3"></div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800 uppercase tracking-wide">Step 1 · Approval</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">Accept or reject each submission. This can be done independently of, and before, assignment below.</p>
        <div id="abstracts-approval-container" class="space-y-4"></div>
      </div>
      <!-- Hidden entirely for a role without abstracts.assign (see
           applyRoleVisibility). The id is on the whole block, not just the
           list, so the heading and blurb go with it rather than leaving a
           section that explains an action you cannot take. -->
      <div id="abstracts-assignment-block" class="pt-4 border-t border-slate-200">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800 uppercase tracking-wide">Step 2 · Assignment (approved abstracts only)</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">Assign oral or poster presentation. The delegate's decision email is sent from here.</p>
        <div id="abstracts-assignment-container" class="space-y-4"></div>
      </div>
      <!-- Step 3, Zenodo (abstracts.publish only, and only while it is
           switched on in Conference setup › Zenodo; renderZenodo()): accepted
           abstracts whose presenting author agreed, sent as drafts with the
           DOI reserved, then published -- which cannot be undone. -->
      <div id="abstracts-zenodo-block" class="hidden pt-4 border-t border-slate-200">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800 uppercase tracking-wide">Step 3 · Publish with DOIs (Zenodo)</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">Only accepted abstracts whose presenting author agreed in the portal, and who has registered. Send as a draft to check it on Zenodo with its DOI reserved, then publish. A published record and its DOI are permanent.</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">Settings and the on/off switch: <button type="button" onclick="switchBackendTab('general'); showSetupPage('zenodo')" class="font-semibold text-indigo-700 underline">Conference setup › Zenodo</button>. <span id="zenodo-status"></span></p>
        <div id="zenodo-summary" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 mb-3"></div>
        <div id="zenodo-list" class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl divide-y divide-slate-100"></div>
      </div>
    </section>
